From 0ebe9bc5e305641b312734cdd25b020d454a8260 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jules Youngberg <julesdayoungberg@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:24:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Finer groups: foley by its files' names, closed hats by
 their folder words

A "file" rule reads the words of a file's own name ("WoodSticksOnConcrete22"), and a
rule's optional fourth element limits it to families holding a word ("foley"). Foley
folders without a material in their name now group as kitchen, metal, wood, plastic,
paper, water, body or sci-fi by most of their files; chains split from metal. Closed
hats split into machine, acoustic, tonal and clicky. A group of one folder now gives
its folder the next group its files say, rather than "other".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
